// Prompts extend the repository rules and disable four of them. Each is
// disabled because ENFORCING it would edit prompt CONTENT, not formatting --
// measured 2026-09-22 by running the fixer and reading its diff (#842).
//
//   MD033 no-inline-html        placeholder notation this project writes on
//                               purpose: <task>, <verification>, <gate>.
//                               115 of the 251 violations. Escaping them
//                               would damage the prompts.
//   MD029 ol-prefix             the fixer renumbered a list that deliberately
//                               started at 5, so "finding 5" silently became
//                               "finding 1". Prompt lists continue sequences
//                               across headings on purpose.
//   MD026 no-trailing-punct     headings in prompts are sentences and end in
//                               a full stop; the fixer deletes it.
//   MD028 no-blanks-blockquote  adjacent quotes separated by a blank line are
//                               two distinct quotations, and this is not
//                               auto-fixable anyway.
//   MD018 no-missing-space-atx  `#713` at line start is an ISSUE REFERENCE, and
//                               CommonMark does NOT treat it as a heading --
//                               a heading needs a space after the hash. The
//                               rule assumes a typo, and its FIX inserts that
//                               space, turning correct prose into an H1. It did
//                               exactly that to `#713` and `#727` here on
//                               2026-09-22 before the diff was read.
//
// Everything else stays ON, including the rules that have actually cost this
// project something: MD013 (the 1000-char cap) and MD018, where a line
// beginning `#833` renders as a heading.
{
  "extends": "../../.markdownlint.jsonc",
  "MD033": false,
  "MD029": false,
  "MD026": false,
  "MD028": false,
  "MD018": false
}
